# Build context for deploy/Containerfile. compose.yaml sets `context: ..`, so
# without this every build streams the whole working tree — a warm `target/`
# alone is gigabytes, and none of it is used: the builder stage compiles from
# source inside the image.
#
# `**/` because a bare pattern here is anchored at the context root: `target/`
# alone left every nested build tree (a crate built on its own, a worktree's)
# in the context. No tracked or vendored path is named `target`.
**/target/
.git/
# Agent worktrees and session state, each a full copy of the tree plus its own
# `target/`: gigabytes, and none of it source.
.claude/
# Local environment files: `.env` and `.env.local` (.gitignore keeps them out
# of git), and `.envrc` and the like. They hold whatever a developer exported
# for a shell, tokens included, and `COPY . /src` would otherwise put them in
# the builder's layer cache. Nothing the build reads starts with `.env`.
**/.env*
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.resume
*.resume.tmp
# The operator's config compose.yaml mounts. It holds the argon2 hash and any
# tokens, and `COPY . /src` would otherwise put it in the builder's layer cache.
deploy/torrentd.toml
